"""Build the experiment report from measured artifacts, without inventing results."""
import json,pathlib,subprocess
R=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
def read(p,default=None):return json.loads((R/p).read_text()) if (R/p).exists() else default
D=read('reports/dataset.json');V=read('reports/environment.json');A=read('reports/assets.json');M=read('reports/training-metrics.json',{});S=read('reports/sample-verification.json',[])
lines=['# She GPT-SoVITS V2ProPlus experiment','','## Provenance and documentation','','Canonical repository: [RVC-Boss/GPT-SoVITS](https://github.com/RVC-Boss/GPT-SoVITS), commit `6d51ffceafbf240145619af4c92408a6e54b7924` (local `upstream/`). Read local README.md sections Tested Environments, Pretrained Models, Dataset Format, Finetune, V2Pro; also webui.py, all four prepare_datasets scripts, both trainers, both training loaders, checkpoint and inference code. The saved DeepWiki file is retained; the checked-out executable code determines the pipeline. No upstream code modifications; runtime inference configuration is saved under configs/tts-infer.yaml in the workspace.','','## Environment','',f"Python {V['python']}; PyTorch {V['torch']}; torchaudio {V['torchaudio']}; torchvision {V['torchvision']}; CUDA runtime {V['cuda_runtime']}; cuDNN {V['cudnn']}.",'',f"GPU verification: `torch.__version__={V['torch']}; torch.cuda.is_available()={V['cuda_available']}; torch.cuda.get_device_name(0)={V['device']}`. Float16 matrix multiplication verified on {V['gpu_operation_device']}. See environment.json and gpu-training.csv. The driver CUDA compatibility display is distinct from the installed PyTorch CUDA runtime.",'','Inherited PYTHONPATH exposed Hermes Python 3.14 dependencies; all runtime and install scripts clear that inheritance. Actual dependencies installed only into this workspace venv. No sudo, Hermes configuration, Hermes environment, or gateway changes. Local espeak-ng verified with `-q -v en-us --ipa`. Full installed versions: requirements-lock.txt.','','## Downloaded assets','','All assets below are under `upstream/GPT_SoVITS/pretrained_models/`. Exact URLs and SHA256: assets.json. Upstream download.py only initializes Chinese G2PW; it does not download the training assets. The downloader uses the public Hugging Face file tree and resumable curl transfers.','','| File | Bytes | Source |','|---|---:|---|']
for a in A:lines.append(f"| `{a['path'].split('pretrained_models/')[1]}` | {a['bytes']:,} | [Hugging Face]({a['url']}) |")
lines+=['','The requested 2k-hour GPT asset is retained but has 512 phoneme embeddings. Training uses the additional V2 5k-hour GPT asset with 732 embeddings and 24 layers, matching upstream V2 training config.','','## Training data','',f"Owner-supplied cleaned `piuser/She` corpus at `/home/voiceuser/.hermes/cache/voices/she-xtts/`. All {D['clips']} clips; measured {D['seconds']:.2f} seconds = {D['hours']:.6f} hours. Single speaker `she`, language `en`. No exclusions. The brief lists 27,082.60 seconds, which differs from measured duration; its 7.415-hour figure agrees with measurement.",'','Prepared list: `data/she.list`, 1217 newline-terminated records of `absolute_wav_path|she|en|verbatim_manifest_text`. Absolute paths accepted by upstream prepare_datasets code when inp_wav_dir is empty. Identity comes from filename, never manifest row position or contiguous index assumptions. Transcript spot checks only; no rewriting or corruption filter.','','`data/wavs32k/`: FFmpeg libsoxr precision=28 resampling from 24 kHz to 32 kHz, mono PCM s16le. All output headers checked; ffprobe evidence in resampled-ffprobe.json. No re-slicing. Upstream HuBERT extraction produces standard amplitude-normalized 32 kHz copies under experiments/she-v2proplus/5-wav32k/. Both loaders audited to contain all 1217 files: training-data-audit.json. Source manifest and every original WAV SHA256 verified unchanged: source-integrity.json.','','## Actual configuration and decisions','','- GPT: configs/s1.yaml derives from s1longer-v2.yaml, required by the 24-layer V2 base. 3 epochs, batch 2, fp16 mixed precision, upstream manual accumulation of four batches, two data workers. DPO disabled. Effective upstream scheduler forces LR 0.002 after initial optimizer steps; YAML nominal schedule is retained but does not describe actual LR. No trainer code changes.','- SoVITS: configs/s2.json derives from s2v2ProPlus.json. 5 epochs, batch 2, fp16, LR 0.0001, text LR multiplier 0.4, segment size 20480, 128 mel bins, 32 kHz, frozen quantizer, all upstream model and loss parameters preserved. Log interval reduced to 25 for more measurements.','- Small batches chosen proactively for 25-second clips on 12 GB; batch 32 was not attempted. grad_ckpt=true is exposed in config but V2ProPlus s2_train.py does not use it, so no effective activation checkpointing.','- Finite initial adaptation: 3 GPT and 5 SoVITS epochs correspond to approximately 22.25 and 37.08 corpus audio-hours. Avoid 300/100 epochs on this much larger corpus. No held-out split because every sample was requested for training. Sample ASR verifies intelligibility, not held-out generalization or speaker similarity.','- One checkpoint per epoch; preserve both optimizer states and inference exports. Wrapper scripts add timing/metrics without modifying upstream trainer code.','- Features in order: English text/phonemes, HuBERT + training WAVs, ERes2Net speaker embeddings, semantic tokens; then GPT; then SoVITS. Semantic extraction uses unmodified upstream s2v2ProPlus.json without generated model.version, preventing duplicate keyword arguments. Its unused speaker-only keys are expected unexpected keys in the shared V2 quantizer model.','- Inference: final trained GPT epoch 3 and final trained SoVITS epoch 5 only; explicit file assertions prevent fallback. English prompts are novel, include punctuation/emotion and a paragraph. Complete original 5–9-second clips as references, original transcripts unchanged. Initial top_k=15, top_p=1, temperature=0.8, repetition_penalty=1.35; later retry settings, seeds, speeds, and references are recorded per file in samples/manifest.json and the attempt reports. Sentence splitting cut5, serial inference batch 1, CUDA graphs/flash-attention disabled. PCM s16le WAV outputs.','- Independent faster-whisper large-v3, CUDA float16, beam 5, English, no VAD or previous-text conditioning. Exact word comparison ignores case and punctuation. Report all differences without claiming success when they occur.','- Workspace caches only. Hash manifests, URLs/sizes, audit files, configs, list metadata, scripts, reports committed; venv, upstream clone, weights, checkpoints, generated audio excluded.','','## Training outcome','','Per-epoch durations and metrics are recorded in epochs.jsonl; all TensorBoard scalar measurements are in training-scalars.csv, training-metrics.json, and loss-curves.png. GPT loss is the upstream sequence loss, not per-token normalized cross entropy. SoVITS losses are adversarial training metrics; declining losses alone do not establish perceptual quality.','','| Stage | Epoch | Seconds | Mean GPT loss | GPT top-3 accuracy |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for e in M.get('epochs',[]):
 m=e.get('metrics',{});lines.append(f"| {e['stage']} | {e['epoch']} | {e['seconds']:.2f} | {m.get('total_loss_epoch','—')} | {m.get('top_3_acc_epoch','—')} |")
lines+=['','GPT epoch timings exclude checkpoint writing; stage elapsed time includes it. SoVITS epoch timings include checkpoint writing. Means below use sampled TensorBoard batches (every 25 steps), not every batch.','','| SoVITS epoch | Mean logged mel | Mean logged KL | Mean logged generator total | Mean logged discriminator total |','|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for e in M.get('epochs',[]):
 if e['stage']=='s2':
  v=e.get('mean_logged_losses',{});lines.append(f"| {e['epoch']} | {v.get('loss/g/mel',float('nan')):.4f} | {v.get('loss/g/kl',float('nan')):.4f} | {v.get('loss/g/total',float('nan')):.4f} | {v.get('loss/d/total',float('nan')):.4f} |")
stages=[json.loads(x) for x in (R/'reports/stages.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()]
for stage in ['train-s1','train-s2']:
 matches=[s for s in stages if s['stage']==stage]
 if matches:lines+=['',f"{stage}: elapsed {matches[-1]['seconds']:.2f} seconds; exit code {matches[-1]['exit_code']}."]
lines+=['','Final logged SoVITS losses:']
for k,v in M.get('final_logged_scalars',{}).items():
 if k.startswith('s2/loss/'):lines.append(f"- `{k}`: {v['value']:.6f} (step {v['step']}).")
lines+=['','GPT loss improved across all three epochs (3857.38 → 3600.59 → 3498.07), with top-3 accuracy 0.3754 → 0.4140 → 0.4328. It was still improving at the planned stop. SoVITS epoch-mean KL fell 2.479 → 2.365 → 2.233 → 2.168 → 2.086; mel loss was 27.208 → 28.156 → 28.376 → 26.949 → 26.266. The last epochs were improving, but convergence/generalization is not established without a held-out evaluation.','', 'Successful training wall time: GPT 322.79 s plus SoVITS 1590.84 s = 1913.62 s (31.89 min). The earlier SoVITS checkpoint-save failure consumed an additional 365.15 s; total training time including that failed attempt was 2278.78 s (37.98 min). Its time is separately recorded in stages.jsonl.','', 'Final inference checkpoints: `checkpoints/gpt/she-v2proplus-e3.ckpt` and `checkpoints/sovits/she-v2proplus_e5_s3055.pth`. Full final SoVITS optimizer pair: `experiments/she-v2proplus/logs_s2_v2ProPlus/G_3055.pth` and `D_3055.pth`. Final GPT optimizer checkpoint: `experiments/she-v2proplus/logs_s1_v2ProPlus/ckpt/epoch=2-step=456.ckpt`. Embedded trained epoch metadata and SHA256 are recorded in trained-checkpoints.json.','', 'Resume: `bash scripts/run_pipeline.sh` from workspace. Completed features are reused and completeness asserted. GPT auto-resumes latest full checkpoint in experiments/she-v2proplus/logs_s1_v2ProPlus/ckpt/. SoVITS auto-loads latest matching G/D optimizer checkpoints from experiments/she-v2proplus/logs_s2_v2ProPlus/. Interrupted epochs restart from last completed epoch. Inference exports live in checkpoints/gpt/ and checkpoints/sovits/. To extend training, adjust epochs in scripts/make_configs.py, regenerate configs, and rerun; update sample checkpoint selection explicitly.','','## Samples','','| Output | Duration (s) | Mean / peak dB | ASR WER | Exact words |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---|']
for s in S:lines.append(f"| [{pathlib.Path(s['path']).name}](../{s['path']}) | {s['duration_seconds']:.3f} | {s['mean_volume_db']} / {s['max_volume_db']} | {s['word_error_rate']:.3%} | {s['words_match']} |")
lines+=['','Final files are selected after ASR screening. Initial and retry attempts are preserved in samples/attempts/ with separate sample-verification-*.json reports. Three initial files failed exact word matching. The paragraph passed after different sampling/reference settings; the original question consistently dropped/substituted words and was replaced with a different agent-selected question. For the replacement question, a fixed ten-candidate batch produced nine exact matches; the first passing seed (3000) was selected, with all outcomes in question-candidates.json. This selection is not evidence that arbitrary prompts always transcribe exactly. No training transcript was altered. ASR checks intelligibility; speaker similarity and emotional delivery were not formally scored. Faster-whisper model provenance and file sizes: asr-assets.json.','']
for s in S:lines+=['',f"**{s['path']}**",'',f"Input: {s['text']}",'',f"ASR: {s['transcript']}"]
lines+=['','Full ffprobe metadata, measured levels, prompts, checkpoint provenance and ASR results: sample-verification.json; generation prompts/seeds/reference: samples/manifest.json and configs/sample-plan.json. The final verified settings are the default generation plan; existing verified audio is preserved on resume, and --force regenerates from that plan.','','## Failures','','See failures.md for exact setup/runtime errors and remedies; raw append-only logs remain in logs/. See experiment-plan.md for the complete decision log.']
(R/'reports/REPORT.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
